        "subject": "LU-20889 tests: check status of each background job",
        "message": "LU-20889 tests: check status of each background job\n\nSeveral tests started commands in the background and then ran\n\"wait || error ...\" or \"wait; rc=$?\" to check them.  \"wait\" without\narguments always returns 0, so a failed job would never be detected.\nconf-sanity test_110 and test_111 ran \"wait $pids\" on several PIDs,\nwhich returns only the status of the last one, so a failure of any\nother job would be missed.\n\nAdd wait_pids() to test-framework.sh to wait for each PID it is given\nand return the status of the first one that failed.  Save the PIDs of\nthe background jobs in sanity test_51b and test_51c, sanityn\ncleanup_81d(), sanity-sec test_48b, performance-sanity test_5a-5d,\nlfsck-performance namespace_gen_one() and conf-sanity test_110 and\ntest_111, and check them with wait_pids() or \"wait $pid\".  Wait for\nthe ofd_access_log_reader PID in sanity test_165a-165g so that its\nexit status is checked.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I2889a6b8e2b1a1e6b64a56efb64a740e323ebbe5\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/70208\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Chakshu Kansal <ckansal@ddn.com>\nReviewed-by: Alex Deiter <adeiter@ddn.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
